' PlantUML file for the Class Diagram in POOSD Assignment #3 with Dr. Aashish Yadavally
' Code written by Adam Betinsky on Wednesday, March 25th, 2026

' START of "class.puml"
@startuml

' Add header to the diagram
header Class Diagram for POOSD Assignment 3 - Adam Betinsky
skinparam HeaderFontColor black

' Deactivate any graphics for icons
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

' Define a class representing a user. All private variables are attributes to each user (with "Login" also being the Username)
class User {
    - ID
    - FirstName
    - LastName
    - Login
    - Password

    + login()
    + logout()
    + addColor() [LOGIN REQUIRED]
    + searchColor() [LOGIN REQUIRED]
}

' Define a class representing a color. All private variables are attributes to each color. Note that "ID" is the ID for the color in the database, and "UserID" is the ID for the user associated with that color
class Color {
    - ID 
    - Name
    - UserID
}

' Define a relationship that every 1 user can have 0 or infinitely many colors in their database
User "1" --> "0..*" Color

' Add footer to the diagram
footer (Note that a "-" indicates a private attribute and a "+" indicates a public attribute)\n (Also, per Dr. Yadavally's advice, I added the basic operations a user can do as public methods to the User class, despite not having those methods in the code itself)
skinparam footerFontColor black

@enduml
' END OF "class.puml"
